# Justified exceptions to script/check-upstream's rules; see docs/upstream-sync.md.
#
# Each line: <path or glob> [hunk=N] [added=N] [removed=N] [any] # <reason>
#   hunk=N     raises the most lines one hunk may add for matching files
#   added=N    raises the most lines matching files may add
#   removed=N  raises the most lines matching files may remove
#   any        allows any change, including adding or removing the file
# The first matching line applies. Keep entries few and the reasons specific.

crates/gpui/src/window.rs hunk=85 added=290 # the frame's hub: one- and two-line hooks for layout keys, retained drawing, phase timing, global ids and the inspector; with Slopty's patches (SLOPTY.md): presented-frame reports, Window::insets, paint_glyph_scaled, the a11y tree for tests
crates/gpui/src/elements/div.rs hunk=165 added=215 removed=30 # Interactivity's listener lists become fast::interactivity::LazyVec, a one-word change per field; the rest are one-line state-version hooks; with Slopty's patches (SLOPTY.md): the outline style, focus falling back to the nearest a11y node, the a11y tree for tests
crates/gpui/src/elements/text.rs removed=160 # TextLayout::layout's body is replaced by fast::text's measurement, which carries measurements across frames and recolors them in place; the method forwards to it
crates/gpui/src/view.rs removed=260 # ViewElement's cache-by-bounds (and the request_layout_view/prepaint_view/paint_view helpers upstream split it into) is replaced by fast::retained's retained views; its Element methods forward to it
crates/gpui/src/taffy.rs removed=50 # request_layout, request_measured_layout and stretch_auto_size_to_fill bodies are replaced by fast::layout's retained nodes; they forward to it

